  "changes": [
    "Ordinary CPU defaults prefer the existing Native selected-byte Gather for plain non-dense storage or F16/BF16 storage. No model, Store association, hardware identity or thread-count qualification is used by this natural rule.",
    "Rank-two axis-zero Gather with contiguous inner payload now copies exact selected rows using their original leading byte pitch. The original full current-ID validation still precedes output write mapping; padding and unselected rows are untouched.",
    "Dense F32/I32 and encoded default routes remain unchanged. Expert Native behavior and existing hardware-qualified kWins remain available.",
    "Default Compute and Graph tests check raw F32/F16/BF16 payloads, odd-width dense/padded rows, current strided IDs, changed selection, NaN/signed-zero bit preservation and invalid-last-ID zero writes. A default-factory padded Gather/Store case checks original lease guards and retirement. The legacy rules assertion is updated for the natural narrow-storage choice."
  ],
